      "text": "b &gt; d &gt; c &gt; a",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "KN6M8",
      "text": "d &gt; b &gt; c &gt; a",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The relative reactivity of alkyl halides in the&nbsp;S<sub>N</sub>1 reaction depends&nbsp;on the stability of carbocation. Electron-withdrawing groups decrease the stability and electron-releasing groups increase the stability of carbocations.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;group is an electron-withdrawing group by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;effect.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>OMe</mi></math>&nbsp;is electron-releasing groups by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;effect. Hence, the overall order is&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/f220809f-4a96-4218-a96c-5d98f428425e-9895989_2.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 241px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Reactivity order (b) &gt; (d) &gt; (c) &gt; (a)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
